            <div xml:id="d945">

                <pb facs="0879" n="789" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg789"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/164</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vologda</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-27T17:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1918, 5
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 29, 10.17 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>209. Wardwell<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d945-f1"/> visited me yesterday; said Red Cross representatives
                    hereafter would confine themselves to relief work, only participating political
                    affairs when requested; gave me confidential verbal message from Radek, who is
                    able influential Bolshevik editor, asking whether I would recommend recognition
                    Finnish independence if Finland would become neutral and sever close relations
                    with Germany; I encouraged suggestion while expressing doubt of its success. Has
                    Department instructions? Finnish-German alliance constitutes great menace to
                    Murman, Archangel, Petrograd, and all European Russia, but means famine in
                    Finland, Archangel Province. Can you communicate with Haynes?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d945-f1" n="1" xml:id="d945-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Allen Wardwell, in charge of the
                    American Red Cross Commission to Russia, See <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_531">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                        p. 531</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
